{
 "subtitle": "The masked family (B1-B3) and the plain baselines: 1.1M env steps, size50m, the same 30 fixed worlds (tools/death_eval.py). Every family run reads the game's rules and counts as cheating. 2026-11-08.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over 30 evaluation episodes, ± its standard error over those worlds; unlock rates are the share of episodes in which an achievement fired; return is the mean raw Craftax return as a % of the maximum (226). Every checkpoint is scored on the same fixed worlds (env.reseed, audit B05), so comparisons are paired world by world. The error bars cover the worlds only, not training seeds.\nThe two plain runs are honest: vanilla DreamerV3 4.63 ± 0.22 and plain DreamerV3 on the fixed code 4.77 ± 0.28. Every other row reads the game's action rules (craftax_valid, a transcription of each action's precondition) and is counted as cheating: B1 gets the 43 validity flags as input (6.30 ± 0.33), B2 masks impossible actions (8.40 ± 0.54; fixed RSSM-2 8.27 ± 0.44, three seeds 8.27 / 7.70 / 9.03, mean 8.33), and B3 learns the mask (5.97 ± 0.28), but still needs the rules in its setup. All family runs also train RSSM-2 on hand-built map labels and use the tech-tree potential shaping, both game knowledge in their own right.\nThe mask is worth +2.63 ± 0.38 achievements against the same model without it (B2 vs the honest map, fixed code, three seeds), and +2.90 ± 0.26 under the v1.2 manager (60 worlds): it is the largest single gain in the project, and it is bought with the rules.",
 "table_note": "ach. ± SE = mean episode-final achievements ± standard error over the 30 worlds (one training seed, so seed variation is not included). w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. return = raw Craftax return, % of 226. Rates are % of episodes. [masked] = impossible actions masked by the rules; [rules] = the rule flags fed to the encoder; [rules in setup] = mask learned from experience, but the env must emit the rule flags to build it, and the basic actions and NOOP are hand-picked. All [..] rows count as cheating. Vanilla: the original checkpoint (code before the 2026-10 fixes), re-scored. Plain: the fixed code, `--configs craftax size50m --env.craftax.survival none`. B1, B2 and B3 ran on the code before the 2026-10-11 RSSM-2 fixes; 'fixed RSSM-2' was retrained after them. B1-B3 sit on the honest-map configuration (RSSM-2 map target, potential shaping); its own runs are on the rssm2 branch.",
