 "interpretation": [
  {
   "heading": "0. The whole family counts as cheating",
   "body": "craftax_valid.valid_actions transcribes every action's precondition from the game's code. B2 reads it while acting, B1 feeds it to the encoder, and B3, which learns its mask from the world model's counterfactual, still needs the env to emit the flags before the head is built, exempts six hand-picked basic actions and treats action 0 as NOOP. The published 1M-step Craftax baselines use none of this. No new work goes on this branch."
  },
  {
   "heading": "1. Masking impossible actions is a large, robust gain",
   "body": "B2 beats the same model without the mask by +2.63 ± 0.38 (fixed code, three-seed mean; +2.23 on the old code) on the same 30 worlds. Under the v1.2 manager removing the mask costs +2.90 ± 0.26 over 60 worlds. Buttons that were never pressed where they would work (the wood pickaxe, the furnace, placing stone) get pressed once a useless press can no longer teach the agent that the button is bad: valid-action suppression (docs/entropy-and-action-suppression.md)."
  },
  {
   "heading": "2. Telling is not masking",
   "body": "B1 sees the same 43 flags as input and scores 6.30, level with the unmasked honest map (6.17) on the fixed worlds; the original evaluation had it 1.0 ahead. Knowing an action is possible does not stop the gradient from pushing it down where it is not."
  },
  {
   "heading": "3. The learned mask failed",
   "body": "B3 (5.97) is level with the honest map and 2.4 below B2. Its labels came from the world model's own latent and its loss trained that latent, so the two fed back on each other: 87% of its 'did something' labels disagreed with the rules. B3-fix (detached, observation-grounded labels) was stopped at 254k steps: its mask let through only 45% of the possible special actions, because the label cannot tell \"does nothing\" from \"not learned yet\". Not scored."
  },
  {
   "heading": "4. The RSSM-2 fixes did not move B2",
   "body": "Retrained after the 2026-10-11 fixes, B2 scores 8.27 against 8.40; its three seeds (8.27 / 7.70 / 9.03) differ by 1.3, more than the fix did."
  },
  {
   "heading": "5. What is left",
   "body": "A knowledge-free mask is the only open idea here: block an action only when a world-model ensemble agrees it does nothing, so an effect not yet learned stays pressable. It would go on a new family branch, without valid_obs."
  }
 ],
